  "findings": [
   {
    "code": "count_mismatch",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "The bundle holds 1.80376e+06 where the producer reported 1.80417e+06 (results.txt: All target PSMs with q-value <= 0.01 (pxreprise:DEF-PSM-1PCT v1)). Both numbers are kept; treat the producer's as canonical until the difference is explained."
   },
   {
    "code": "low_core_use",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "14.72 avg cores of 32 allowed (S5)"
   },
   {
    "code": "occupancy_not_stored",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Of 387241 occupancy entries MetaMorpheus wrote, some are not in ptm_stoichiometry: 14793 site not in ptm_sites. 'site not in ptm_sites' means the entry's site has no ptm_sites row to key on; 'not determinable' means a cell's segments could not be assigned to its accessions from the sequences (QuantProject DEF-OCC-ACCESSION), which is never guessed. Absence of a row for these sites is therefore not NA. A 'duplicate' is a second entry for a (site, run) that already has a row: one with identical values loses nothing; one with DIFFERENT values means MetaMorpheus wrote two answers and the first in file order was stored (examples in bundle.json occupancy.differing_duplicates; which one should be stored is QuantProject's to define)."
   },
   {
    "code": "peptide_rows_localization_ambiguous",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "768 row(s) of AllQuantifiedPeptides.tsv name several full sequences, joined by `|`: a peptide whose modification site the search did not settle (MetaMorpheus #2917). Their 4452 value(s) are not stored, since storing them under one of the sequences would place them on a site the search never decided. The PSMs behind them are in `psms`. E.g. `AADEVAEGKLNDHFPLVVWQTGSGTQ[Common Artifact:Deamidation on Q]TNMNVNEVISNR|AADEVAEGKLNDHFPLVVWQ[Common Artifact:Deamidation on Q]TGSGTQTNMNVNEVISNR|AADEVAEGKLN[Common Artifact:Deamidation on N]DHFPLVVWQTGSGTQTNMNVNEVISNR`, `AADEVAEGKLNDHFPLVVWQ[Common Artifact:Deamidation on Q]TGSGTQ[Common Artifact:Deamidation on Q]TNMNVNEVISNR|AADEVAEGKLN[Common Artifact:Deamidation on N]DHFPLVVWQTGSGTQ[Common Artifact:Deamidation on Q]TNMNVNEVISNR|AADEVAEGKLN[Common Artifact:Deamidation on N]DHFPLVVWQ[Common Artifact:Deamidation on Q]TGSGTQTNMNVNEVISNR`, `AADK[Trypsin Digested:GG (Ubiquitination Site) on K]D[Metal:Potassium on D]TC[Common Fixed:Carbamidomethyl on C]FSTEGPNLVTR|AAD[Metal:Potassium on D]K[Trypsin Digested:GG (Ubiquitination Site) on K]DTC[Common Fixed:Carbamidomethyl on C]FSTEGPNLVTR`."
   },
   {
    "code": "sdrf_uncoded",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "The deposited SDRF describes its samples only as text with no ontology term, so the curated organism part, cell type, disease and individual columns are empty. The text is in sample_characteristics: organism part: heart. Match on it as text; it has not been mapped to a term."
   },
   {
    "code": "unplaced_ptm_sites",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Some modifications on peptides shared between proteins were not written to ptm_sites for one or more of those proteins, because the peptide could not be located in that protein's sequence and the producer's residue spans cannot be paired with its accessions. Of the (PSM, protein) pairs affected: 7757 named a protein that does not contain the stored peptide -- typically a PSM ambiguous between peptide sequences (level 4 or 5), where this protein carries a different candidate than the first, which is the one stored. Sites on the other proteins of the same PSMs are written. Counts are in bundle.json under protein_databases."
   },
   {
    "code": "occupancy_decoy_groups",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "99 occupancy entries on decoy protein groups were not stored: MetaMorpheus computes them, and they are FDR machinery, not biology."
   }
  ],
